# CODEOWNERS — auto-requests reviewers on every PR (GitHub-native).
#
# WHY the toolkit requires this: the pr-review-loop reviews PRs where the operator
# is a REQUESTED reviewer, and it refuses to review a PR authored by the operator
# (self_pr — you can't review your own work). The build loops (spec/implement) author
# PRs as the operator's `@me`. So for the autonomous review chain to work, GitHub must
# auto-request a reviewer who is NOT the loop's author.
#
# THE RULE: the reviewer(s) named here MUST be a different identity than whoever the
# build loops author PRs as. GitHub never requests review from the PR author even if
# they are a code owner — so if the loop authors as <op> and <op> is the only owner,
# NO reviewer is requested and pr-review-loop finds nothing. Name a teammate (or a
# team) other than the loop operator.
#
# SETUP:
#   1. Replace <reviewer> below with the GitHub handle (@user) or team
#      (@org/team) that reviews this repo — NOT the loop's author account.
#   2. Point pr-review-loop's `github_user` at that same reviewer, and run the
#      pr-review-loop under that reviewer's `gh` auth (so its review posts as them).
#   3. (Optional) enable branch protection "Require review from Code Owners" to
#      enforce it.
#
# Default: every file is owned by the reviewer (whole-repo review). Narrow to paths
# (e.g. `src/ @backend-team`) as the team grows.

